    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0105" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363/250: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-10T17:00:00-06:00">March 10, 1943—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>208. Refer Legation’s strictly confidential despatch 1431 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">1441</hi>], February 25,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d92-f1"/>
                    reporting negotiations by Señor Madrigal, President of the Banco de Brazil
                        Nacional,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d92-f2"/> for the importation of 50,000
                    gallons of gasoline from Mexico.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d92-f3"/></p>
                <p>I have today been asked by Mr. Jorge Escalante, head of the Costa Rican Gasoline
                    Rationing Board, if such importation should be made whether there will be a
                    corresponding reduction in the regular quota allotted for delivery to Costa Rica
                    by the Latin American Supply Committee.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d92-f4"/> It is
                    understood that the importation in question would be made in bulk and would be
                    merely the first of regular shipments.</p>
                <pb facs="0106" n="92" xml:id="pg92"/>
                <p>Since Señor Madrigal is now in Mexico arranging this deal, it is urgent that I be
                    informed immediately whether all petroleum importations outside the pool will be
                    deducted from pool deliveries.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d92-f1" n="1" xml:id="d92-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d92-f2" n="2" xml:id="d92-f2-content">
                <p>Actually Ramón Madrigal Antillon was president of the Banco Nacional de Costa
                    Rica.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d92-f3" n="3" xml:id="d92-f3-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning petroleum exports from Mexico, see letter of August
                    31 from the Ambassador in Mexico, and instruction No. 4606, October 23, to the
                    Ambassador in Mexico, <ref target="#pg463">pp. 463</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg465">465</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d92-f4" n="4" xml:id="d92-f4-content">
                <p>The Petroleum Supply Committee for Latin America, with headquarters in New
                    York.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
